{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I gave the Levites.</b> Since they have given themselves of their own accord to My service, I gave them to My service — to Aaron and to his sons." "<b>to perform the service of the children of Israel in the Tent of Meeting.</b> To perform that service which had been fitting for their firstborn." "<b>and to make atonement for the children of Israel.</b> Through their receiving the tithes from Israel so that they may serve the blessed El, they make atonement for Israel — all of whom bore responsibility in the matter of the calf, which caused Him to reject their firstborn." "<b>and there shall be no plague among the children of Israel.</b> Neither among the Levites nor among the rest of Israel." "<b>when the children of Israel approach the sanctuary.</b> For in this the unauthorized persons who approach will sin, and the Levites who allow the unauthorized to approach will all incur guilt, as it says: וְלֹא יָמֻתוּ גַּם הֵם גַּם אַתֶּם (Numbers 18:3)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:04.296078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}